---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Welcome to Astro.">
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl space-y-4 p-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold sm:text-2xl">Hei, what's up?</h2>
    <p class="sm:text-lg">
      I'm Francisko, a <span class="text-mocha-pink">front-end developer</span> based
      in Minas Gerais, Brazil.
    </p>
    <p class="sm:text-xl">
      <span class="text-mocha-yellow"
        >A long time ago in a galaxy far, far away</span
      > I used to be a biologist. Eventually I realised it wasn't quite I what I
      wanted, so I made a career transition into IT.
    </p>

    <p class="sm:text-lg">
      Now I develop performant, accessible, websites and apps using <span
        class="text-mocha-pink">TypeScript</span
      >, <span class="text-mocha-pink">React</span>, and <span
        class="text-mocha-pink">Next.js</span
      > (I used Astro for this one though, pls don't tell Lee Rob). Besides sweating
      profusely every October when Vercel launches a new Next major version with
      breaking changes, I'm dipping my toes on the backend side of things by learning
      <span class="text-mocha-sky">Go</span>.
    </p>

    <p class="sm:text-lg">
      I'm planning on using this blog as way to document my learnings, hope
      someone finds it useful :)
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>

